       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. Single doses above about 1,000 mg are not typical.\n- **Risk:** 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose at a different frequency\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
